      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is abstraction?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Abstraction hides complex implementation details and exposes only essential features, reducing complexity for the user."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Abstraction focuses on what an object does rather than how it does it. Achieved through abstract classes and interfaces. Helps manage complexity in large systems."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Abstraction Example",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "public interface IPaymentProcessor {\n    bool ProcessPayment(decimal amount);\n}\npublic class CreditCardProcessor : IPaymentProcessor {\n    public bool ProcessPayment(decimal amount) {\n        // Complex logic hidden\n        return true;\n    }\n}"
      }
    },
    {
